# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/

# Custom
.venv
**/*.draft.json
CONCEPT.md
FINDINGS.md
REVIEW.md
TODO.md
# Official BDEW/BNetzA/DVGW source documents (copyrighted, ~400 MB).
# Indexed by regulatories/README.md with the download URL for each file.
#
# The *index* is tracked, so the mirror can be reconstructed from a fresh clone.
# Neither tracked file carries copyrighted content: the README is the hand-kept
# list of BNetzA/DVGW sources with their download URLs, and the manifest is
# generated by `cargo xtask sync-regulatories` — upstream ids, validity windows
# and content hashes for the BDEW half.
#
# Tracking the manifest is what makes `sync-regulatories --offline` and the
# `validate-profiles` source-citation guard work in CI, where the PDFs are
# absent. Without it both silently pass.
#
# The patterns exclude directory *contents* rather than the directories: git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is itself excluded.
regulatories/*
!regulatories/README.md
!regulatories/bdew-mako/
regulatories/bdew-mako/*
!regulatories/bdew-mako/manifest.json
concepts/
.DS_Store
.github/skills
.claude

# Zola build output
/site/public

# Python / maturin build artefacts (makotest)
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.so
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
*.egg-info/
.venv/

# Node tooling for the docs site (site/tools/check-mermaid.mjs)
node_modules/
site/package-lock.json

# maturin leaves the debug-symbol bundle beside the built extension.
*.dSYM/
